    "result_text": "The full suite is green. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Change: `customerCode` assignment on owner creation\n\nThe `POST /api/owners` OfficeFloor pipeline now assigns each owner a `customerCode` formatted `<LAST3>-<NNNN>`.\n\n**New pipeline step** \u2014 `AssignCustomerCode.java`, wired into `owners.POST.yml` between `build` and `save` (under the same `transaction` governance), so the owner being created is *not* counted in its own sequence:\n- `LAST3` = upper-cased first three letters of `lastName` (clamped for short names)\n- `NNNN` = `ownerRepository.findAll().size() + 1`, zero-padded to 4 digits \u2014 a global sequence one more than the current owner count (e.g. `SMI-0007`)\n\n**Persistence & exposure** so `GET /api/owners/{id}` returns the value:\n- `Owner` entity: added the persisted `customerCode` field (`customer_code` column) with getter/setter\n- `openapi.yml`: added `customerCode` as a read-only property of the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct maps it by name (no mapper change needed)\n- Schema DDL: added `customer_code` to `owners` in the hsqldb, h2, mysql and postgres schemas, and appended the trailing column value to the positional hsqldb seed inserts\n\n**Tests:** `AcceptanceTest.coreFormatAndGlobalSequence` passes (verifies the `SMI-`/`JON-` prefixes and that the global sequence increments by one between two creates), and the full `./mvnw test` build is green.\n\nOne note: the mysql seed `data.sql` uses positional `INSERT ... VALUES` that was already short one column before this change, so I left it as-is \u2014 it isn't exercised by the test profile (hsqldb).",
